  "title": "Sounds, greetings and courtesy",
  "note": "Italian is spelled almost exactly as it sounds. C and g are hard before a, o, u and soft before e, i; adding h (ch, gh) keeps them hard. Use tu with friends and family and Lei with strangers or in formal settings.",
